  "chain_verdict": "The out buffer of the RE-015 flag-group chain is owned in three stages. Each format's buffer is allocated by the format consumer 0x141e3a0 itself: it sizes a capacity from its template scan, allocates it through the alloc slot (0x64df480 -> 0x6355830), builds the 24-byte header {capacity, pointer, 0} on its own stack, formats into it through the write target, and copies the whole header into its caller's out slot. The callee 0x15ae430 receives those headers in its own scratch slots, and delivers the second format's header into its caller's out slot. The terminal owner is the large consumer 0x15a3b90: all four of its callee calls pass the same stack slot [rsp+0x158] as the out argument (on the non-format paths the large consumer prefills that slot itself with an allocated copy stored as {size, pointer, size}), and after the calls it moves the header out of the slot into its sorted-node map -- on a walk hit, into the found entry's 24-byte triple, freeing the replaced buffer through the dealloc slot under the sentinel guard; on a miss, verbatim into the value record of the map insert call 0x156d840. The chain never frees the delivered buffer itself: ownership passes to the map entry.",
  "captured_code_executed": false,
  "limits": "Out-buffer ownership for the RE-015 flag-group chain only: the large consumer 0x15a3b90 stack out slot at [rsp+0x158] (its complete 18-access census, the four callee call setups that pass its address, the two inline prefill windows, and the two post-call consumption windows per segment -- the sorted-node map hit store with the replaced buffer's guarded free and the miss path's insert-record build), plus hash-pinned boundary FDEs whose construction and delivery sites are re-pinned but whose full traces are owned by the sibling packets (the format consumer 0x141e3a0's buffer construction by the flag-group-format packet, the callee 0x15ae430's scratch delivery by the derived-byte-callee packet). The map insert function 0x156d840, the allocator/deallocator targets behind slots 0x64df480/0x64df4a0, the map root's own provenance and lifetime beyond the large consumer, the value the map handle register holds on the format paths, and every other caller of the format consumer are NOT traced. No captured code executed, no runtime value, indirect-call recovery beyond the pinned slot bindings, #94 correspondence, or reconstruction gate is claimed."
